---
const steps = [
  {
    title: "1. Pick games you love",
    text: "Search the library and add the games you have already played.",
  },
  {
    title: "2. We build your taste profile",
    text: "Each game is turned into a vector from its description, genres and tags. Your profile is the average of the games you picked.",
  },
  {
    title: "3. Similar games are ranked",
    text: "Candidates are found with vector search, then re-ranked by shared tags and rating, so good games rise to the top.",
  },
  {
    title: "4. You see why",
    text: "Every result shows the game you played that it is most similar to, plus a match score.",
  },
];
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-24 border-t border-white/10 py-20 text-[var(--white)] md:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="mb-9 max-w-2xl">
      <p class="section-kicker mb-3">Under the hood</p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.045em] md:text-5xl">Good matches have a reason.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-[var(--white-icon)]">
        GameMatch combines semantic similarity with shared tags and ratings, so
        each recommendation is more than a popularity ranking.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {
        steps.map((step, index) => (
          <li class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-5">
            <span class="mb-8 block text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--sec)]">0{index + 1}</span>
            <h3 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold">{step.title.replace(/^\d+\.\s*/, "")}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--white-icon)]">{step.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
